    "result_text": "All 11 tests pass, build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a `displayName` field to owners, formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema (which the OpenAPI generator turns into a getter/setter on the generated `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that populates `displayName` via the expression `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`.\n\n**Why this approach:** Both the create (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and read (`RespondWithOwner`) responders serialize through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so deriving the value in the mapper means the created owner carries `displayName` and it's also visible on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read-back that the test uses to verify it. It's derived from the *stored* names (the entity's getters, after any normalization), exactly as specified. Keeping it read-only means the reverse mapping ignores it.\n\nThe new `Cp05Tests` passes and the full suite is green (11/11, `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
